# The backup bundles under _bk/ are byte-exact records of what was published,
# and each one ships a SHA256SUMS.txt so anyone can prove nothing was altered.
#
# Git's line-ending conversion would quietly break that: on a fresh clone it
# rewrites LF to CRLF in text files, every byte-count shifts, and every
# fingerprint in SHA256SUMS.txt stops matching the file beside it. The record
# would still be readable, but it would no longer be provable -- which is the
# only reason the fingerprints are there.
#
# -text turns that conversion off for these folders. Nothing else in the
# repository is affected.
_bk/** -text
